  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/ctrl1/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. P4 review 2026-11-01 at dev 9ae4abe13f: 3 surveys of a py+js fixture. Sorted node ids, stable_ids, edge ids and (pass, run_signature) pairs were identical (same hash) across all 3, so the L2 contract holds. But with the item's five fields removed and the three arrays sorted, the runs are no longer byte-identical: analysis_runs[].cpu_ms (added 704ffe3b9e, after filing) varies, and so does the ORDER of limits.skipped_passes[] (scheme/racket/scss/matlab/robot moved around). Both are already in WI-sazap's 11-01 scope. The control has no work left, so it can close. MECHANISM: content-derived identities (node id/stable_id, edge id, run_signature) are deterministic; run-to-run churn is in provenance/timing fields and in the order of limits.skipped_passes[] (emitted in thread-completion order). SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-sazap WI-situf. PROPOSED DISPOSITION: close (awaiting owner authorization; status unchanged)."  # ffd9
